Q242148 | food, technology | pakistan | Mehrgarh, on the Kacchi Plain of Balochistan near the Bolan Pass, is a Neolithic and Chalcolithic site where a small farming village began around 7000 BCE. | Mehrgarh is one of the oldest farming villages in South Asia. People there grew wheat and kept animals about 9,000 years ago.
Q9443 | trade, technology | west | Lothal, in the Bhal region of Gujarat, was one of the southernmost sites of the Indus Valley Civilisation. Construction is believed to have begun around 2300 BCE. | Lothal was a town of the Indus people in what is now Gujarat. It is more than 4,000 years old.
Q1068408 | power, religion | north | The Kuru kingdom, a union of the Bharata and Puru tribes in northern India, appeared in the Middle Vedic period, about 1200 to 900 BCE. | The Kuru kingdom was one of the first kingdoms of northern India, in the time when the Vedas were being composed.
Q112980583 | power | pakistan | Gandhara was an Iron Age kingdom of north-western South Asia. Its people were called the Gandharis. | Gandhara was an old kingdom in the north-west of South Asia.
Q234009 | power | gangetic | Magadha was a region and kingdom based in the eastern Ganges Plain. It was one of the sixteen Mahajanapadas of the second period of city-building. | Magadha was a kingdom beside the river Ganges. Later, great empires grew out of it.
Q756854 | power | gangetic | Kosala was one of the Mahajanapadas of ancient India. It emerged as a small state during the Late Vedic period. | Kosala was one of the sixteen big states of ancient northern India.
Q4827705 | power | central | Avanti was a Mahajanapada roughly corresponding to today's Malwa region. Buddhist texts list it among the sixteen great states. | Avanti was a kingdom in central India, in the region now called Malwa.
Q605199 | power | gangetic | The Vajjika League, also called simply Vajji, was an ancient Indo-Aryan tribal league or confederacy. | The Vajji were a league of clans who joined together.
Q1330149 | power | north | Surasena was an ancient region corresponding to today's Braj in Uttar Pradesh, with Mathura as its capital. | Surasena was an old kingdom whose capital was the city of Mathura.
Q1331184 | power | gangetic | Vatsa, or Vamsa, was one of the sixteen Mahajanapadas named in the Buddhist text Anguttara Nikaya. | Vatsa was one of the sixteen great states of ancient India.
