Q112108709 | war, power | gangetic | In a war of about 540 to 535 BCE, the Haryanka dynasty of Magadha defeated the neighbouring Anga kingdom. | Long ago the kingdom of Magadha fought its neighbour Anga and won. Magadha was starting to grow.
Q389755 | power, daily | gangetic | Pataliputra, beside today's Patna, was first built by the Magadha ruler Ajatashatru in 490 BCE as a small fort near the Ganges. | The great city of Pataliputra began as a small fort by the river Ganges in 490 BCE. Today the city of Patna stands next to it.
Q98078069 | war, power | gangetic | In the Magadha–Vajji war, the Haryanka dynasty of Magadha fought the neighbouring Vajjika League, which was led by the Licchavis. | The kingdom of Magadha went to war with the Vajji league of clans next door.
Q5071385 | trade, daily | east | Chandraketugarh, a cluster of villages in the Ganges Delta about 35 km north-east of Kolkata, is an archaeological site of ancient Bengal. | Chandraketugarh is a place in Bengal where archaeologists have found the remains of a very old town.
