Q213074 | war | pakistan | At the Battle of the Hydaspes in May 326 BC, the Macedonian army of Alexander the Great fought the Pauravas under King Porus on the river now called the Jhelum. | In 326 BC Alexander the Great fought King Porus beside the Jhelum river.
Q786725 | power, movement | pakistan | Boukephala and Nikaia were two cities founded by Alexander the Great on either side of the Hydaspes, today's Jhelum River, during his invasion. | Alexander founded two new towns on the banks of the Jhelum river after his battle there.
