Q62943 | power | gangetic | The Maurya Empire, with its power base in Magadha, was founded by Chandragupta Maurya around 320 BCE and lasted until 185 BCE. | Chandragupta Maurya founded the first empire to rule most of India, more than 2,300 years ago.
Q7447941 | war, power | pakistan | Between 305 and 303 BCE Seleucus I Nicator, ruler of the Seleucid Empire, crossed the Indus and confronted the Maurya Empire. | Seleucus, ruler of the Seleucid Empire, crossed the river Indus and met the army of the Mauryas.
Q151148 | power | south | The Chola dynasty was a Tamil dynasty of southern India. At its height it ruled an expansive maritime empire. | The Cholas were a family of Tamil kings in the far south of India. Much later they built a great empire of the sea.
