Q184427 | arts, religion | deccan | The Ajanta Caves are 30 rock-cut Buddhist cave monuments in Maharashtra, made between the second century BCE and about 480 CE. They are a World Heritage Site. | At Ajanta, Buddhist halls were cut into a cliff and painted with beautiful pictures. The work went on for more than 600 years.
Q5257 | power | deccan | The Satavahanas, called the Andhras in the Puranas, were an ancient Indian dynasty of the Deccan. | The Satavahana kings ruled the Deccan, the high land in the middle of India.
