Q1255614 | power | pakistan | The Indo-Parthian kingdom, known as the Pahlavas in Sanskrit texts, was founded by Gondophares I in the first century CE. | A king named Gondophares founded a kingdom in the north-west that mixed Persian and Indian ways.
Q25979 | power, trade | afghanistan | The Kushan Empire, about 30 to 375 CE, was formed by the Yuezhi. First based in Bactria, it spread across much of today's Afghanistan, Pakistan and northern India. | The Kushans built an empire that stretched from Afghanistan deep into India.
Q2086608 | power | west | The Western Satraps, or Western Kshatrapas, were Indo-Scythian (Saka) rulers of the western and central parts of India. | The Western Satraps were Saka kings who ruled western and central India.
